<div class="page">

  <h1 class="hl">The Top 5 Tick &amp; Insect Repellents of 2026 &mdash; And the One We Can No Longer Live Without</h1>
  <p class="dek">Tick season isn't what it used to be &mdash; and most repellents only guard the skin you remember to cover. We compared how each one actually works, and how it holds up over a real season outside.</p>

  <div class="byline">
    <span class="by-l">
      <span class="av" role="img" aria-label="Wade Patterson"></span>
      <span>Written by <strong>Wade Patterson</strong><br class="m-br"> on <span id="psDate"></span><br>Outdoor Health Writer</span>
    </span>
    <span class="readtime"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/><path d="M12 7v5l3 2"/></svg> 4 min read</span>
  </div>

  <div class="heroimg"><img src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/1009/5601/2725/files/Six_Products_Lineup_White_Background.png?v=1784508777&width=1000" alt="The five repellents we tested this season" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" width="1000" height="558"></div>

  <div class="body">
    <p>The numbers are ugly this year. ER visits for tick bites are at <strong>record highs</strong> &mdash; and ticks aren't just in the deep woods anymore. They're in backyards, city parks, and the grass behind your kid's school.</p>
    <p>And one bite is all it takes. Lyme can quietly hollow you out &mdash; <strong>fatigue, aching joints, brain fog</strong> &mdash; and a single lone star bite can leave you allergic to red meat for life.</p>
    <p>So the repellent you pick actually matters. We ranked the five most common ones on <strong>how they really work and how long they last</strong> &mdash; not on marketing. Here's what we found.</p>
  </div>

  <h2 class="sec">How We Ranked These Repellents</h2>
  <div class="body">
    <p><strong>Whole-Body Coverage.</strong> Does it protect all of you at once, or leave gaps a tick can slip through?</p>
    <p><strong>Protection Window.</strong> How long does one application actually keep working before it fades?</p>
    <p><strong>Family Safety &amp; Ease.</strong> Is it clean and simple enough to use on the whole family, day after day?</p>
    <p><strong>Real-World Results.</strong> Do the people using it actually get through a season without dealing with tick and insect bites?</p>
  </div>

  <h2 class="sec">Our Top 5 Tick &amp; Insect Repellents</h2>

  <!-- ============ #1 PINEMOOR ============ -->
  <div class="rcard">
    <div class="rhead">
      <h3 class="win">#1 &mdash; Pinemoor&reg; Tick-Protection Drops</h3>
      <svg class="medal" viewBox="0 0 100 100"><defs><linearGradient id="gold1" x1="0" y1="0" x2="0" y2="1"><stop offset="0" stop-color="#f8e08a"/><stop offset=".5" stop-color="#eec24a"/><stop offset="1" stop-color="#d69a24"/></linearGradient></defs><g fill="#e6b93b"><ellipse cx="27" cy="54" rx="4" ry="7.5" transform="rotate(-38 27 54)"/><ellipse cx="23" cy="45" rx="4" ry="7.5" transform="rotate(-18 23 45)"/><ellipse cx="23" cy="35" rx="4" ry="7.5" transform="rotate(4 23 35)"/><ellipse cx="73" cy="54" rx="4" ry="7.5" transform="rotate(38 73 54)"/><ellipse cx="77" cy="45" rx="4" ry="7.5" transform="rotate(18 77 45)"/><ellipse cx="77" cy="35" rx="4" ry="7.5" transform="rotate(-4 77 35)"/></g><circle cx="50" cy="44" r="25" fill="url(#gold1)" stroke="#c88f1c" stroke-width="2"/><circle cx="50" cy="44" r="19" fill="none" stroke="#fff" stroke-opacity=".45" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="50" y="54" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--display),Arial" font-size="27" font-weight="800" fill="#8a5f12">1</text></svg>
    </div>
    <div class="tiles">
      <div class="tile"><img src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/1009/5601/2725/files/Pinemoor_Bottle_No_Badges.png?v=1784508933&width=440" alt="Pinemoor Tick-Protection Drops" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="440" height="440"></div>
      <div class="tile"><span class="t-label">Overall Grade</span><span class="t-grade">A+</span></div>
      <div class="tile"><span class="t-label">Rating</span><span class="t-rating">9.1<small>/10</small></span><span class="t-stars">&#9733; &#9733; &#9733; &#9733; &#9733;</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="inner">
      <p>Pinemoor took #1 &mdash; and it's the first of its kind. Instead of a spray you reapply all day, it's <strong>eight drops of a maple-sweet formula you add to your morning coffee or juice.</strong> It works from the inside out, so there's no patch to miss and nothing to reapply &mdash; <strong>one morning dose covers the whole day.</strong> (Mosquitoes lock onto the same cues, so it keeps them off, too.)</p>
      <p>And it's no watered-down "natural" spray. Its concentrated actives &mdash; carvacrol, thymol, and geraniol &mdash; <strong>out-repelled DEET, permethrin, and picaridin head-to-head in published lab assays,</strong> and carvacrol kills ticks on contact.</p>
      <p>Best of all, it's <strong>family-owned</strong> &mdash; 100% organic, odorless, third-party tested, kid-safe, 4.8 stars across 1,206 reviews, and a Lifetime Money-Back Guarantee.</p>
      <div class="bars">
        <div class="bar-row"><span class="bar-label">Whole-Body Coverage</span><div class="bar-track"><div class="bar-fill" style="width:94%"></div></div><span class="bar-score">9.4/10</span></div>
        <div class="bar-row"><span class="bar-label">Protection Window</span><div class="bar-track"><div class="bar-fill" style="width:88%"></div></div><span class="bar-score">8.8/10</span></div>
        <div class="bar-row"><span class="bar-label">Family Safety &amp; Ease</span><div class="bar-track"><div class="bar-fill" style="width:91%"></div></div><span class="bar-score">9.1/10</span></div>
        <div class="bar-row"><span class="bar-label">Real-World Results</span><div class="bar-track"><div class="bar-fill" style="width:89%"></div></div><span class="bar-score">8.9/10</span></div>
      </div>
      <p class="pc-h pros">PROS</p>
      <div class="pc"><svg viewBox="0 0 26 26" fill="none"><circle cx="13" cy="13" r="11.5" stroke="#3F7A4F" stroke-width="2"/><path d="M7.5 13.5l3.5 3.5 7-8" stroke="#3F7A4F" stroke-width="2.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> Works from within &mdash; one morning dose, no reapplying</div>
      <div class="pc"><svg viewBox="0 0 26 26" fill="none"><circle cx="13" cy="13" r="11.5" stroke="#3F7A4F" stroke-width="2"/><path d="M7.5 13.5l3.5 3.5 7-8" stroke="#3F7A4F" stroke-width="2.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> Actives out-repelled DEET, permethrin &amp; picaridin in lab assays</div>
      <div class="pc"><svg viewBox="0 0 26 26" fill="none"><circle cx="13" cy="13" r="11.5" stroke="#3F7A4F" stroke-width="2"/><path d="M7.5 13.5l3.5 3.5 7-8" stroke="#3F7A4F" stroke-width="2.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> Family-owned small business &mdash; organic, odorless, kid-safe</div>
      <p class="pc-h cons">CONS</p>
      <div class="pc"><svg viewBox="0 0 26 26" fill="none"><circle cx="13" cy="13" r="11.5" stroke="#9E3B1F" stroke-width="2"/><path d="M8.5 8.5l9 9M17.5 8.5l-9 9" stroke="#9E3B1F" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg> Only available online &mdash; not on store shelves</div>
      <div class="pc"><svg viewBox="0 0 26 26" fill="none"><circle cx="13" cy="13" r="11.5" stroke="#9E3B1F" stroke-width="2"/><path d="M8.5 8.5l9 9M17.5 8.5l-9 9" stroke="#9E3B1F" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg> Frequently sells out during peak tick season</div>
      <p class="bl"><strong>Bottom Line:</strong> The one product here that protects from within instead of from a bottle &mdash; concentrated, clean, and backed by a Lifetime Guarantee.</p>
      <p class="offer-line">Pinemoor Extended Up To 45% OFF + Free Gifts for Our Readers (Likely to Sell Out)</p>
      <a class="visit" href="https://pinemoor.co/products/double-potency-upgrade-ultimate-tick-protection-1-bottle?view=pinemoor-v2">VISIT SITE</a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ============ #2 OFF! ============ -->
  <div class="rcard">
    <div class="rhead">
      <h3>#2 &mdash; OFF!&reg; Deep Woods &amp; Family Care</h3>
      <svg class="medal" viewBox="0 0 100 100"><defs><linearGradient id="sil2" x1="0" y1="0" x2="0" y2="1"><stop offset="0" stop-color="#f4f4f4"/><stop offset=".5" stop-color="#d0d0d0"/><stop offset="1" stop-color="#a9a9a9"/></linearGradient></defs><g fill="#cfcfcf"><ellipse cx="27" cy="54" rx="4" ry="7.5" transform="rotate(-38 27 54)"/><ellipse cx="23" cy="45" rx="4" ry="7.5" transform="rotate(-18 23 45)"/><ellipse cx="23" cy="35" rx="4" ry="7.5" transform="rotate(4 23 35)"/><ellipse cx="73" cy="54" rx="4" ry="7.5" transform="rotate(38 73 54)"/><ellipse cx="77" cy="45" rx="4" ry="7.5" transform="rotate(18 77 45)"/><ellipse cx="77" cy="35" rx="4" ry="7.5" transform="rotate(-4 77 35)"/></g><circle cx="50" cy="44" r="25" fill="url(#sil2)" stroke="#a3a3a3" stroke-width="2"/><circle cx="50" cy="44" r="19" fill="none" stroke="#fff" stroke-opacity=".5" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="50" y="54" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--display),Arial" font-size="27" font-weight="800" fill="#707070">2</text></svg>
    </div>
    <div class="tiles">
      <div class="tile"><img src="{{ 'pm-4650001842-c5bde.webp' | asset_url }}" alt="OFF! Deep Woods" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="440" height="440"></div>
      <div class="tile"><span class="t-label">Overall Grade</span><span class="t-grade" style="color:#18382A">B+</span></div>
      <div class="tile"><span class="t-label">Rating</span><span class="t-rating" style="color:#18382A">7.4<small>/10</small></span><span class="t-stars">&#9733; &#9733; &#9733; &#9733; <span class="off">&#9733;</span></span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="inner">
      <p>Chances are you already have OFF! sitting in your garage, and <strong>it genuinely does repel insects decently well, for the most part.</strong> Deep Woods has decades of reputation behind it for a reason.</p>
      <p>But it's a DEET formula &mdash; and DEET is a <strong>solvent strong enough to melt plastic watch faces and fishing line.</strong> That's why anglers keep it off their gear, yet it's exactly what you're rubbing on your arms and your kids all day.</p>
      <p>Coverage is the other gap. It guards the patch it lands on and nothing else, so a tick routes around the strip you missed &mdash; and lately, more people report getting bitten even on skin they'd already sprayed. It also carries the usual chemical smell and a greasy film in the heat.</p>
      <p>And it's on a clock. Protection thins out after a few hours &mdash; faster when you sweat &mdash; so a real day outside means re-spraying at lunch, then again at dinner.</p>
      <div class="bars">
        <div class="bar-row"><span class="bar-label">Whole-Body Coverage</span><div class="bar-track"><div class="bar-fill" style="width:48%"></div></div><span class="bar-score">4.8/10</span></div>
